sections={
'A':('Distance, demand and fare calibration','How do fares and support vary across distance?','Counts, means and quantile bands use saved half-kilometre bins. The current [1.5,75) km population is distinct from the [1,75) reference-price origin. No reference is recomputed.'),
'B':('Denominator and population resolution','What changes when near-reference fares are unresolved?','The frozen inclusive 5% relative-price screen excludes 353,234 from runtime consideration; 834,708 resolved negative observations are also excluded. Historical rows remain retained. Before/after nonnegative views have different N; no absolute-value sign conversion occurs.'),
'C':('Sensitivity distribution selection','Which representation preserves held-out empirical shape?','Empirical resampling is best supported. Saved fits compare Gamma, Weibull, Lognormal and Exponential on a common internal random-row split. These pooled-marginal diagnostics remain valid, but pooled-only runtime has been superseded by conditional lookup.'),
'D':('Weather/time conditioning','How does each actual weather/time cell select support?','T1 has G1={1,2,3,5,7,8,9,12,14,16}, G2={13,15}. Codes17/21 have fallback handling. T2–T4 use T-pooled support. T1_G2 N=1,669 is below runtime N≥5,000; eligible raw-code fallback is used. SD<4 is not a hard grouping gate. Missing observations are not imputed. The original linkage matrix was not saved; D5 remains missing.'),
'E':('Passenger ceiling and feasible actions','Which offers are model-feasible, and which are served?','P_raw=P_base+(P_base/epsilon)r_L; P_accept=max(0.85 P_base,P_raw). Seven actions enforce the 1.15 P_base maximum offer. No raw-preference upper clipping occurs. Feasibility is not assignment. Request plots use the frozen highest-feasible export, with identical sensitivity fixture but policy-dependent fleet state.'),
'F':('End-to-end implementation','Where do pricing, routing and learning interact?','The diagram separates training replay/Bellman updates from March16 greedy inference. CNN/routing are frozen during pricing; this is request-level masked DQN, not the historical MAB formulation.'),
'G':('Training and development traces','Is there evidence of learning or convergence?','Training revenue/assignment trends mix source conditions and cannot establish policy improvement. Loss is per training episode; saved Q/TD/action trajectories are checkpoint development diagnostics, explicitly labelled. Per-training action counts were not persisted. No convergence claim is supported.'),
'H':('Controlled development comparisons','How does Episode25 compare on the fixed day?','All policies use the same 73,754-request March16 fixture. Episode25 earns $1,237,868.21 on59,632 assignments; Highest Feasible earns $1,261,843.09 on59,768. The gap is −$23,974.88 (−1.90%) and−136 assignments. Development results are not final holdout performance.'),
'I':('Action position and stability','How often does the learned policy choose below the feasible maximum?','Of27,719 choice requests, 43.00% select highest,40.86% one below and16.14% two or more below. EP20→25 choice-action agreement is41.0801255%. Fixed-development checkpoint agreement is incomplete; top-line rewards alone do not establish stability.'),
'J':('Q calibration','Do network values match realized return?','Episode25 mean selected Q is about160.05 versus mean Monte-Carlo return1,675.51. Request-level Q/MC pairs were not persisted, so the optional scatter is unavailable. Dynamic-case Q ranking is incorrect19 times with1 undiscounted tie; all20 discounted comparisons are unfavorable.'),
'K':('Dynamic opportunity and realized value','Can lower prices change future state, and is that beneficial?','The full-day screen finds meaningful immediate divergence. Twenty genuine divergent cases persist across routing boundaries, with one partial recovery, one full recovery and zero net-positive cases. Chronological bounded sampling omits peak-demand quartile and is not a prevalence estimate or proof of universal Highest Feasible dominance.'),
'L':('Correctness and provenance','What has been validated?','Saved overlapping suites have zero failures/errors; do not sum counts. Resume accounting, fixture identity and paired controls are documented. This reporting run performs no simulation or model execution.'),
'R':('Routing learning context','What evidence supports the frozen routing model?','The existing temporal routing update norm and CE traces are reused. Regression MSE requests are inapplicable to the current classification loss. Routing remains frozen during the V2 pricing experiment.')}
